[#:seon.task{:name "contract-attributes"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Give `seon.fs/attributes` a complete Malli contract that checks what its boundary is for, with the cheapest schema that checks it (`docs/seon/architecture/contracts-guide.md`): registered names, every input and output, the error variants it returns. A contract that refuses a real value (a reaching test, a live call, your probe) is a finding, not friction: if the contract misread the value's shape, fix the contract and cite the observed shape; if the producer emits a bad value, keep the contract, file a task on the producer naming `seon.fs/attributes` in its must-read with the exact form, the refused value's essence and the Malli explain, and say so in your reply. Never widen to :any, [:maybe ...] or :map to go green. A caller that passes nil to an input is the producer of the bad value: change the caller so it does not pass nil (absence is no key), or take a map with the key optional; never contract nil with [:maybe ...] or :nil. Done when `seon.contracts/gaps` answers [] for it and its reaching tests stay green and no slower."
             :must-read #{seon.fs/attributes seon.contracts/gaps}
             :evidence #{"docs/seon/architecture/contracts-guide.md"}}]
